  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14238243/assets/a9c9324b8b15e38c1037d39a744a9e1d28796ea70a5d300563f9eaaaef966522.png)\n\nIdentify the equation that generated the graph shown above.",
  "worked_solution": "To obtain the given graph, we perform the following transformations:\n\n- Take the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}.$\n\n- Translate the graph down by $5$ units to get the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}-5.$\n\nThe result is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14238243/assets/f005ef005ce79b953aa61c01266ab4b9ba39c215169faf833bd91529f0e99c77.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $y=\\sqrt{x}-5.$",
